  "ownership": "The parked supervisor borrows the existing helper wait future. A reported child exit or stdout error is not retirement: terminate and quiesce_recovering retain original child/stdout/encoder settlement gates before returning. No new resource, retry task, frame buffer or callback cycle is allocated. Cancellation leaves the same existing owners and original completion tickets authoritative; fresh helper admission still uses restart_ready. The parked path clears codec headers and remembered encoder mode, and does not admit capture without current demand. Eventual cleanup depends on original native workers settling. Tests own private helper children and current async output futures; timeout/panic retains the existing child/task cleanup sponsors.",
  "scope": "Two failing-first tests observe original completion and clear retained state before any demand notification. Two stream integration tests verify fresh helper, codec headers and IDR on resume after child exit or stdout failure. These are private process/socket/FIFO tests, not physical compositor or tablet acceptance. Installed sessions untouched.",
